Equivalents </I></B></FONT></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT STYLE="font-family:Times New Roman" SIZE="2">The Company considers all short-term, highly liquid investments that are readily convertible to cash with
a maturity of three months or less at the time of purchase to be cash equivalents. Cash equivalents may include cash and short-term investments. Short-term investments are stated at cost, which approximates fair value. There were no restrictions on
the use of the Company&#146;s operating cash balance, as of December&nbsp;31, 2008, and for the six months ended June&nbsp;30, 2009. </FONT></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT STYLE="font-family:Times New Roman"
SIZE="2">In conjunction with the contribution of the real estate assets, see Note 3, the Company assumed certain reserves, held by the lender, to be used for specific property improvements. As of June&nbsp;30, 2009, the balance of these reserves,
